            %p
              This implies that the transgression of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi BFV
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \Omega_{BFV}
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+field+histories"} space of field histories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Σ
                          %mi tra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi EL
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_{\Sigma_{tra}}(E)_{\delta_{EL}\mathbf{L} = 0}
              vanishes (since by definition
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EquationOfMotionEL"} (?)
              that involves pulling back through the shell inclusion)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Σ
                          %mi tra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi BFV
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
